\begin_layout Standard
\paragraph_spacing single
\align block
The advancement of artificial intelligence (AI) features on flagship smartphones in 2025 necessitates a recommendation system that integrates user opinions with objective specifications.
 This research develops an AI-based smartphone recommendation system that combines sentiment analysis of X platform (Twitter) users with device specifications using the Twitter-RoBERTa model.
 The dataset comprises 13,343 English-language tweets collected via Apify Twitter Scraper from five flagship smartphones:
 Samsung Galaxy S25 Edge,
 iPhone 17 Air,
 Xiaomi 15 Ultra,
 Vivo X200 Pro,
 and OnePlus 13.
 AI feature detection employs a rule-based two-pass detection approach to identify four primary features:
 AI Camera,
 AI Virtual Assistant,
 AI Face Recognition,
 and AI System Optimization.
 The pre-trained Twitter-RoBERTa model classifies sentiment into three categories (positive,
 negative,
 neutral) with 52.5% accuracy and Cohen's Kappa of 0.795.
 Results indicate positive sentiment of 44.4%,
 neutral 45.3%,
 and negative 10.2%.
 Xiaomi 15 Ultra leads with a sentiment score of 86.1 out of 100.
 The recommendation system integrates three score components (sentiment 40%,
 specification 30%,
 preference 30%) to generate personalized recommendations.
 An interactive website displays a sentiment dashboard,
 smartphone catalog with 4D information (Dimension,
 Design,
 Display,
 Durability),
 a Three.js-based 3D model viewer,
 and a personal recommendation system.
 This research demonstrates that integrating social media user sentiment with technical data produces more comprehensive and personalized product recommendations compared to purely technical data-driven methods.
\end_layout

